<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout:</strong> Fairly heavy test log.</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> The SCP is a gun store named ‘Gun-thers Armory’ owned by '(Name Pending. Maybe MC&amp;D.)'. It has all the amenities you would expect (Firing Room, Break Room, etc). It is open at almost all hours, closing at 23:30 on Saturday, and reopening at 0:00 on Sunday. Every time the store is reopened, there will be 1 firearm inside a glass case that is anomalous. The glass case will not restock until the store closes and reopens. It also has some other minor anomalous properties, such as an indestructible shooting gallery, a fridge in the break room that always has some food in it (even if it was previously empty).</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> After finding several anomalous arms throughout the local area, the foundation traces the guns back to the store. They investigate the store under the guise of “Safety Inspectors”. They attempt to shut down, buy out, or overall, limit public action, but every time they try, within a few hours, it is reverted. This is found to be due to the fact that the company has a seemingly endless supply of funds and resources. They investigate the place’s 1 worker who works there for the entire time (anomalously severe case of insomnia lets him work all week.). The guy considers it as irrelevant to talk about his job outside of work, so the foundation just puts a mic on their glasses to monitor them. As for the store itself, the foundation try to make the minor anomalies seem normal to the public, and just buy the anomalous gun the second the store opens. There will be test logs for the weapons. MTFs are allowed to use any weapons created, excluding those deemed unsafe for usage by the ethics committee, those ineffective for what the foundation requires from their weaponry, or those who have too minor an effect to replace standard issue weaponry. Eventually, the foundation shuts down the store by just demolishing it. They have to relocate the firing range.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> TBD</p>

